@startuml sequence_diagram_backend_integration
autonumber
title WEB01 - UC2: read and update a product through REST

actor "LaPrizza Manager" as User
participant "Product page (WEB05)" as Page
participant "productApi (WEB05)" as Adapter
participant "ModuleRequest" as Request
participant apiClient as Client
participant "Back-End API (BCK05)" as API

note over Page, API
Proposed WEB05 integration using the existing BCK05 REST contract.
The product ID comes from the API and is reused for read, write and refresh.
The API checks the caller's permissions on every request.
end note

User -> Page : Open the product selected from the list
Page -> Adapter : getById(productId)
Adapter -> Request : request(GET, /products/{encoded productId})
Request -> Client : request(GET, path, { accessToken })
Client -> API : GET /api/v1/products/PROD-00001 (Bearer)
alt Read succeeds
  API --> Client : 200 ProductResponseDTO
  Client --> Request : Parsed DTO
  Request --> Adapter : DTO
  Adapter --> Page : DTO
  Page --> User : Display the product and edit form
else Not found, denied or unavailable
  opt API sent an error response
    API --> Client : HTTP error
  end
  Client --> Request : ApiError
  ref over Request, API : Recheck current roles on 401 / 403; no replay (SD3)
  Request --> Adapter : Original ApiError
  Adapter --> Page : ApiError
  Page --> User : Explain failure and do not open the edit form
end

opt Product loaded and manager submits a valid form
  User -> Page : Save edited product
  Page -> Adapter : update(product.id, updateBody)
  note right of Adapter : PUT uses the complete writable BCK05 body.\nThe ID remains in the path.
  Adapter -> Request : request(PUT, /products/{encoded productId}, { body })
  Request -> Client : request(PUT, path, { body, accessToken })
  Client -> API : PUT /api/v1/products/PROD-00001 (Bearer + JSON)
  alt Write succeeds
    API --> Client : 200 ProductResponseDTO
    Client --> Request : Parsed DTO
    Request --> Adapter : DTO
    Adapter --> Page : Confirmed save
    ref over Page, API : Re-read the saved product by the same ID\nusing the GET chain above
    Page --> User : Show saved data, or explain if the refresh failed
  else Write rejected or response unavailable
    opt API sent an error response
      API --> Client : HTTP error
    end
    Client --> Request : ApiError with status and kind
    ref over Request, API : Recheck current roles on 401 / 403; no replay (SD3)
    Request --> Adapter : Original ApiError
    Adapter --> Page : ApiError
    alt Business or validation rejection (e.g. 400 / 409)
      Page --> User : Show reason and keep unsaved input where appropriate
    else Access no longer valid
      Page --> User : Hide protected content as required
    else Outcome unconfirmed (timeout, network or 5xx)
      Page --> User : Re-read saved data before any manual retry
    end
  end
end
@enduml
